course: dictionary
lesson: 14441
title: Palate: the roof of your mouth and your taste
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A palate has two meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one. In a science lesson about the body, your palate is the roof of your mouth. «The doctor looked at the roof of Sam's mouth and checked his palate.» Here it is a part of the body.
explain: In food talk, a palate is your sense of taste and the foods you like. «Mia has a sensitive palate, so spicy curry makes her cough.» Mia's palate is not a body part here. It means how her tongue and taste react to food.
explain: Ask yourself: is the sentence about a body part, or about food and taste? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If «the roof of Mia's mouth makes her cough» does not make sense, you know which meaning fits.
fact: A palate is a noun: a palate, palates.
fact: Your palate is the roof of your mouth.
fact: The hard palate is at the front of the roof of your mouth, and the soft palate is at the back.
fact: A person's palate is their sense of taste and what foods they like.
fact: «Please the palate» means to be tasty and pleasing to eat.
exercise: «The doctor looked at the roof of Sam's mouth and checked his palate.» What is a palate here? | A flat dish for dinner | Your tongue | Your teeth | *The roof of your mouth
exercise: «Mia has a sensitive palate, so spicy curry makes her cough.» What does palate mean here? | Her loud voice | Her favourite plate | *Her sense of taste | Her hard bones
exercise: Which palate is at the front of the roof of your mouth? | *Hard palate | Your gums | Soft palate | Cleft palate
test:
«Ben's palate loves salty crisps, but he hates sour lemons.» What does palate mean in this sentence? | *His sense of taste and what foods he likes | The roof of his mouth | A plate for his crisps | A kind of sweet cake
test:
Which part of the mouth is the soft palate? | The front of the roof of your mouth | *The back of the roof of your mouth | Your tongue | Your lips
exam:
«Gran's apple pie was so good that it pleased every palate at the table.» What does pleased every palate mean? | *Made everyone enjoy the taste | Made everyone fall asleep | Made the table break | Made the plates go dirty
